WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.740
The critics have spoken—and they do not
like Suicide Squad.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.280
"Love your perfume, what is that the scent
of death?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.800
Ha ha ha!"

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.230
But audiences showed up anyway, proving once
again that franchise tentpoles do not necessarily

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.439
live and die by their critical reception.

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:24.429
That doesn't mean moviegoers loved everything
they saw, though.

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:29.999
As Jared Leto puts in his bid to appear in
Ben Affleck's standalone Batman flick, let's

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:34.070
take a look at what fans think of Jared Leto's
Joker.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:40.109
"Ha ha ha ha ha aahhhhh"

00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:41.789
Laughable Behavior

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:47.320
The story of Leto's on-set antics made headlines
before Suicide Squad's debut.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:52.789
He's a method actor, so he isolated himself
from the rest of the cast, surfacing only

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:56.030
to send his co-stars bizarre gifts.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.679
"I can't wait to show you my toys"

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:05.640
When it comes to rats, bullets, and dead hogs...amongst
other things...he's apparently very generous.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.400
His behind-the-scenes behavior generated a
lot of hype around his seemingly zany performance,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.240
making it a point of major curiosity—especially
since Leto is known to be very selective about

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.560
his acting gigs.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.710
However, many were underwhelmed by his performance.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:26.560
And one consistent complaint has been that
Leto's portrayal was too over the top.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.920
The Joker is classically a wild card, but
after Jack Nicholson's work in Tim Burton's

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.310
Batman, and the legendary interpretation that
Heath Ledger offered in Christopher Nolan's

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.540
The Dark Knight, Leto's work was almost exasperating
for those that didn't like it.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.960
Long Walk For A Short Joke

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.159
Another common complaint, even from those
who didn't love Leto's part in the movie,

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:53.860
is that he didn't get enough face time in
the flick.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.530
Leto has said that many of his scenes were
left on the editing room floor, which seems

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:04.700
accurate since he's barely in the movie despite
being such a central part of the film's promotional

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.700
campaign.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:11.290
Some fans said they saw more of him in his
music video appearance than the movie itself,

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.750
which was disappointing, although not exactly
his fault.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.700
Twitter Titters

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.760
Not everyone disliked Leto's Joker.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:24.570
A quick glimpse at social media reveals plenty
of fans who enjoyed his unique energy, and

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.239
who were happy to see a new take on the character.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:30.280
An unexpected thread amongst fans of Leto's
Joker?

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.980
That he was damn sexy in the role.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:38.920
For some filmgoers, Leto remains a handsome
man, and no amount of grillz or wacky tattoos

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.849
can take that away.

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:42.280
Creepy Cut-Up

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:47.540
Another notch in the plus column for Leto
as Joker: the fact that he was, at times,

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.489
pretty chilling to watch.

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:54.580
Considering he wasn't even the main villain,
he still managed to freak audiences out, making

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.450
good use of his limited screen time.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.799
The Last Laugh

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:04.360
Leto hasn't yet reached icon status as the
Joker in Suicide Squad thanks to his brief

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:09.879
screen time and the mixed fan reactions to
his work in the role, but it wasn't a total

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:10.879
wash, either.

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:16.340
Given a little more time and material, Leto
could still go down as one of fans' favorite

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.310
Jokers in cinematic history.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:23.890
This movie didn't do that for him…so maybe
a turn as the resident supervillain in Affleck's

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.410
standalone feature is in order after all.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.569
Thanks for watching!

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.709
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:35.349
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you thought of Jared Leto's Joker...

